{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/630862-changing-breeds-stats","id":630862,"title":"changing breeds stats","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-18T02:18:32-07:00","id":630862,"title":"changing breeds stats","content":"I don't know I anyone already talked about it, but I strongly think that the forms stats of the changing breeds are... unbalanced towards the animal breeds.<br /> I mean, a werehyena in crinos gain +4 in stamina and a wereshark...+2 like a Ratkin?<br /> A chasmus-wereshark (I'm talking about a tiger or a white shark BIGGER than an avarage normal shark...) gain +..3 in stamina?<br /> That's a little bit ridiculous...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T07:13:27-07:00","id":631147,"title":"","content":"Rokea definitely need some changes, but the Crinos and Crinos-analogs aren't a place where predictable and familiar measures should be expected. Those forms are a particular type of nightmare come to life, in a metatextual sense, which is why a lot of breeds were beefier in their near-beast forms instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T08:25:32-07:00","id":631209,"title":"","content":"The stats aren't really supposed to be &quot;balanced&quot;. This is The World of Darkness, remember? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> On the other hand i whole heartedly agree that someone really cocked up the stamina on the Rokea. Those things are paragons of persistance and survival, yet they get comical stamina values. Pish-posh, Smithers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T10:14:31-07:00","id":631282,"title":"","content":"I don't really agree that balance isn't something to be strived for. Years and years ago (when I had a lot more free time) I had re-written all of the form bonuses for all of the changing breeds with balance in mind.<br /> It worked out well enough. There was plenty to be moved around to allow for &quot;balanced&quot; forms. Adding dots to perception or accounting for additional form abilities also got factored in.<br /> <br /> I wholeheartedly agree that form stats really do need some work, but it is worth keeping in mind that there are just going to be some things that don't add up outside of the animal forms, since the battle forms have stats that have to do with a breeds purpose. That's part of why Garou end up with the stats they do, even though wolves are &quot;weaker&quot; than some other animal changers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T10:31:19-07:00","id":631297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/630862-changing-breeds-stats?p=631209#post631209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The stats aren't really supposed to be &quot;balanced&quot;. This is The World of Darkness, remember? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> !</div> </div> </div> </div>And you're right , no doubt, but you know.. If we talk about a great white shark being bigger and terrible, and a rat being bigger and terrible I think there is something missed about some stats, like you said, stamina for example. I agree with this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but it is worth keeping in mind that there are just going to be some things that don't add up outside of the animal forms, since the battle forms have stats that have to do with a breeds purpose. That's part of why Garou end up with the stats they do, even though wolves are &quot;weaker&quot; than some other animal changers. </div> </div> </div>Yes, the garou are the warriors of Gaia, and they need those stats but.. again, even a ratkin gain +2 in stamina.. like a great-white-6 meters long-killing machine ?<br /> I'm not talking about balance ok, see it from another angle: I'm talking about logic.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T12:18:48-07:00","id":631397,"title":"","content":"The Powers That Be were (and are) leery about given appropriate &quot;whoomp'em&quot; stats, for fear of feeding the PwrGmrz too much of what they crave: da' dice, man! --<i>Da' Dice!</i> #TwinksAreGonnaTwink<br /> <br /> I agree, conceptually, with the OP. Some bonuses simply need to be whoomp'em where appropriate, and the sharks should get a scary spread.<br /> <br /> Don't hold your breath, though, waiting for TPTB to do it -- houserule that shit and move on....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T13:14:03-07:00","id":631457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/630862-changing-breeds-stats?p=631297#post631297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the garou are the warriors of Gaia, and they need those stats but.. again, even a ratkin gain +2 in stamina.. like a great-white-6 meters long-killing machine ?<br /> I'm not talking about balance ok, see it from another angle: I'm talking about logic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do actually agree with this point. Though it is worth pointing out that a &quot;typical&quot; great white adult is 11-13 feet (about 4 meters). I agree more than +2 stamina makes sense, but you can't go too high with it either. Each dot of attribute covers a lot of range.<br /> I seem to remember giving Rokea +2/+2/+2 for Squamus stats, with an additional 2 or 3 points to be put into attributes depending on breed type.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T02:56:06-07:00","id":632110,"title":"","content":"The stats are like they are because they were written by different people through a long period of time. Some of them got changed, and others did not along the way. We can still see the baggage of some authors splat love overinflating stats (Bastet), and other authors trying to stay within more sensible limits or even erring on the side of lower stats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T03:17:05-07:00","id":632124,"title":"","content":"Yup, W20 Bastet versus CB20 Bastet is interesting to see.<br /> I think it was conveniently left out in CB20 that Ratkin in Rodens get these stamina boni, but they cannot use these extra dice when soaking damage from bladed weapons, firearms, or the teeth and claws of supernatural creatures (breed book, p. 63). That put the strangely generous modifiers back into perspective a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/593/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3312-taci","name":"Taci","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3312_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}